verdict.deployNotes:
Nothing is pushed, merged or deployed. App branch: fix/integration @ dc85ab3 (/fast/aibeaty-fix/integration); all 15 test files pass there, but assistant-live-smoke.js was skipped. The stand is on :4199 with a fresh DB. Landing: /fast/aibeaty-fix/landing @ 8a05620, a separate repo; the preview is on :4184.

Deploying fix/integration would be a large improvement over the current production app. It still should not go in front of real clients until one short lane closes 4 small items:
(a) a holding reply to the client and an owner alert for every inbound message while a human is handling the conversation;
(b) preview conversations never lock (automatic hand-back or a separate test mode), and the preview notice follows the chat language;
(c) preview test bookings do not hold real slots and are left out of revenue and the digest;
(d) the Luminous Core dashboard, schedule and performance screens are hidden or unlinked for self-serve tenants.
Also run assistant-live-smoke.js once before release.

The landing can ship on its own once the owner confirms the policy lines (30-day deletion, 7-day pause for an unpaid invoice, no partial refunds, 'we don't train on client messages'). It also needs a line naming INNOVA CONSULT LTD as the billing entity near the pricing/CTA, because signup and step 7 do not show it.

Owner decisions still open: card checkout (turn on the Stripe keys) or invoice-only; whether Google Calendar sync and Instagram DM go into the trial; Canadian hosting or a DPA for the medspa/Pro tier; a short vanity chat link (e.g. aibeaty.ca/s/<slug>).

Integration known risks: merge conflicts were already resolved (the pickText rename, the data-owner-qr fix). Owner-facing llm_error and daily-cap notes are still partly Russian.
